<html
  lang="en"
  class="light"
>
  <script>
    try {
      if (localStorage.getItem('theme') === 'dark') {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('light');
        document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
      }
    } catch(e) {}
  </script>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    />
    <meta
      name="robots"
      content="noindex"
    />
    <title>Reading at scale takes a key · Bitblocks</title>
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href={~p"/assets/app.css"}
    />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <main
      id="payment-required"
      class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
    >
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
        402 Payment Required
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
        Reading at scale takes a key
      </h1>
      <p
        id="payment-required-why"
        class="mb-3"
      >
        {@why}
        The free budget opens again in
        <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{@retry_after_s}</span>
        seconds.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-8">
        A key is free to get, and gives you a budget of your own.
        Heavy use is paid.
      </p>

      <ol
        id="payment-required-ways"
        class="space-y-6"
      >
        <li id="way-sign-in">
          <a
            href={@sign_in_path}
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
          >
            Sign in with GitHub
          </a>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
            Signed in, you read with
            <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{@signed_in_budget}</span>
            requests a minute of your own.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li id="way-free-key">
          <a
            href="/start"
            class="font-semibold text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Get a free API key
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm">
            Sign a challenge with a wallet, and the key comes back at once, with no account.
            Send it on every request as <code class="font-mono">Authorization: Bearer bbk_…</code>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li id="way-plans">
          <a
            href={@plans_path}
            class="font-semibold text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
          >
            Plans for heavy use
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm">
            Reading the chain at scale is paid: a plan raises your key's budget.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li
          :if={@x402}
          id="way-x402"
        >
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            For agents: pay per request with x402
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm">
            This response carries a <code class="font-mono">PAYMENT-REQUIRED</code> offer.
            Sign it with an x402 client, and send the same request again with a <code class="font-mono">PAYMENT-SIGNATURE</code> header.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li
          :if={@bsv}
          id="way-bsv"
        >
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            For wallets: pay per request in BSV
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm">
            This response carries <code class="font-mono">x-bsv-sats</code> and <code class="font-mono">x-bsv-server</code>, as BRC-121 describes.
            A BRC-100 wallet, or <code class="font-mono">@bsv/402-pay</code>, pays them and sends the same request again.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        Questions, or a data license:
        <a
          href={"mailto:#{@contact_email}"}
          class="underline text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >{@contact_email}</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
